WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
Audiences were hungry for Netflix's new&nbsp;
series on Jeffery Dahmer – but no one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.540
asked what the people involved in the real-life&nbsp;
case would think about the series, until now.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.980
The sheer number of movies and television&nbsp;
series on the subject indicates that people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.140
have a twisted affection for serial killers.&nbsp;
Hollywood has long been cashing in on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.720
stories of some of humanity's worst people, and&nbsp;
the true crime boom has only fanned the flames.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.520
In the last few years, we've seen two films&nbsp;
about the notorious serial killer Ted Bundy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.200
alone: "Extremely Wicked, Shockingly&nbsp;
Evil, and Vile" and "No Man of God."

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:40.680
However, when it comes to television, it seems no&nbsp;
killer has been as high-profile as Jeffrey Dahmer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:46.440
2017's "My Friend Dahmer" looks at the Milwaukee&nbsp;
Monster's coming of age, and the documentary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.940
series "Conversations with a Killer: The Jeffrey&nbsp;
Dahmer Tapes" recently debuted on Netflix.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:56.520
Most recently, the murderer and sex offender&nbsp;
is the subject of "Dahmer — Monster:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.320
The Jeffrey Dahmer Story." The series has&nbsp;
hit a significant milestone for Netflix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.660
quickly surpassing 300 million hours&nbsp;
viewed. Still, "The Jeffrey Dahmer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.820
Story" has its share of critics, many of whom&nbsp;
are the relatives of Dahmer's victims. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.300
those families have begun to speak&nbsp;
out about the divisive series.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.980
"The Jeffrey Dahmer story is&nbsp;
so much bigger than just him."

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.960
Despite the immense popularity of "Dahmer —&nbsp;
Monster: The Jeffrey Dahmer Story," the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.060
has received its share of backlash. Some headlines&nbsp;
were in response to a production assistant who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.320
claimed on-set conditions were traumatizing,&nbsp;
while others pushed back against Netflix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:40.440
initially tagging the series as an "LGBTQ" story.&nbsp;
But most damning has been the reaction from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:46.080
victims' families, many of whom have condemned the&nbsp;
series for being retraumatizing and exploitative.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.160
In a piece for Insider, Rita Isbell&nbsp;
— whose brother, Errol Lindsey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.080
was murdered by Dahmer in 1991 — denounced&nbsp;
Netflix for failing to reach out to her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.460
even though they recreated her victim's&nbsp;
impact statement in the widely-viewed series.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.120
"I don't ever want to have to see&nbsp;
my mother go through this again."

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:04.500
She said,

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.540
"I was never contacted about the show. I&nbsp;
feel like Netflix should've asked if we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:14.220
mind or how we felt about making it. They&nbsp;
didn't ask me anything. They just did it."

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.080
Isbell also added, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.480
"It's sad that they're just making money&nbsp;
off of this tragedy. That's just greed."

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:26.160
Eric Perry, whom the New York Times described&nbsp;
as a relative of the Isbells, agreed, saying,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.720
"It's retraumatizing over and&nbsp;
over again, and for what? How&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.600
many movies/shows/documentaries do we need?"

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.400
While series co-creator Ryan Murphy has a&nbsp;
reputation for creating violent and dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.460
series like "American Horror&nbsp;
Story," many believe that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:45.360
series' creators should have taken much&nbsp;
more care with this particular story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.100
taking into consideration the real pain and&nbsp;
suffering of the families of Dahmer's victims.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:55.020
Eric Wynn, a former performer at Club 219 in&nbsp;
Milwaukee, where Dahmer frequently visited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.340
also criticized the series' existence in an&nbsp;
interview with the New York Times. He said,

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:04.320
"It couldn't be more wrong, more&nbsp;
ill-timed, and it's a media grab."

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.500
For Wynn, who personally knew&nbsp;
some of Dahmer's victims,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.340
the series is especially disappointing&nbsp;
coming from creator Ryan Murphy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.680
who also created the inclusive, joyful&nbsp;
series "Pose." Wynn, who is Black, said,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:23.100
"I was so impressed; we finally had representation&nbsp;
that we were involved in. And then he turns around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:27.720
and does this, somebody who is actually&nbsp;
attacking the Black gay community."

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.280
Murphy reportedly set out to tell Dahmer's&nbsp;
story with the victims at the center,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.700
a point which actors on the&nbsp;
show emphasized during media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:40.080
appearances. Star Evan Peters described&nbsp;
the series to Netflix Queue by saying,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:45.540
"It's how society and our system failed to&nbsp;
stop him multiple times because of racism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.200
and homophobia. Everybody gets&nbsp;
their side of the story told."

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:55.380
But for at least some of the victims' families,&nbsp;
the series failed to meet that goal. Of Dahmer's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:01.080
years-long reign of terror over the queer&nbsp;
community in Milwaukee, Wynn said, "That's a scar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:06.780
on our city." But for some of those closest to&nbsp;
the case, it's a wound that still hasn't healed.

